{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqbbndrgd1k","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"NEW PROBLEM: bench KB-dependency is non-reproducible because the live KB is a moving target","summary":"Surfaced by the full-suite smoke [[note-mqbbfla22pq]] (2026-06-12, user-diagnosed). A bench candidate designed to be KB-DEPENDENT (OFF fails, KB rescues) implicitly assumes a STABLE targeting note in the live KB. But the self-learning loop CHURNS the KB — supersession + dedup/consolidation rewrite a note's content, embedding, and therefore its gate-features (top1/gap/locality/empirical-class). Evidence: task-transcript's calibration note note-mq7kyiir6sx was superseded 5x (→ note-mqa12hw637x → mqa16klgs77 → mqa1dtbxirw → mqa3vbpct2c CURRENT), the current one re-phrased as an 'OVERRIDE:' note with different vocabulary. So a candidate that WAS KB-dependent at calibration time silently stops triggering the same gate decision later — the gate was tuned on the original note's features, not the churned one. CONSEQUENCE 1 (bench): KB-dependency isn't reproducible run-to-run; the smoke found 0 KB-dependent candidates partly because the targeting notes drifted. CONSEQUENCE 2 (production, deeper): the learned gate's training rows (note-state, decision, outcome) go STALE as notes churn — not just embed-model drift (already version-stamped) but CONTENT drift via the loop's own consolidation. FIX DIRECTION: (a) bench candidates must SEED their own candidate-specific targeting note fresh from the OFF-arm failure (the bench-lift method already in KB) rather than depend on ambient live KB — makes KB-dependency self-contained + reproducible; (b) optionally pin/snapshot the KB for a bench run; (c) for production, the learner needs note-churn awareness (stamp note-version/supersession-id on journal rows, or re-derive features as-of decision time). SEPARATE BUG also seen: task-transcript's gated arm returned gate=null/no-gate (the gate did not EXECUTE — zero output tokens, not a threshold 